1
00:00:00,182 --> 00:00:03,305
The SAT gives you a math reference sheet.

2
00:00:03,325 --> 00:00:05,555
But it mostly covers shapes.

3
00:00:05,575 --> 00:00:09,341
Algebra and advanced math are about
seventy percent of the section,

4
00:00:09,361 --> 00:00:12,039
and almost none of their
formulas are on it.

5
00:00:12,111 --> 00:00:13,182
Those are on you.

6
00:00:13,214 --> 00:00:15,087
First, here's exactly
what is on the sheet,

7
00:00:15,107 --> 00:00:17,500
so you don't waste time memorizing it.

8
00:00:17,607 --> 00:00:23,607
Then, fifteen formulas that aren't,
each with a quick SAT-style example.

9
00:00:23,632 --> 00:00:25,061
Here's the whole sheet.

10
00:00:25,311 --> 00:00:27,791
Area and circumference of a circle.

11
00:00:27,811 --> 00:00:30,596
Area of a rectangle and a triangle.

12
00:00:30,632 --> 00:00:34,112
The Pythagorean theorem, and
the two special right triangles:

13
00:00:34,132 --> 00:00:37,255
thirty, sixty, ninety, and forty-five,

14
00:00:37,275 --> 00:00:38,989
forty-five, ninety.

15
00:00:39,033 --> 00:00:42,228
Volumes of a rectangular prism, cylinder,

16
00:00:42,248 --> 00:00:44,049
sphere, cone, and pyramid.

17
00:00:44,069 --> 00:00:48,121
And three facts: a circle has
three hundred sixty degrees,

18
00:00:48,141 --> 00:00:53,371
or two pi radians, of arc, and a triangle's
angles add up to one hundred eighty

19
00:00:53,391 --> 00:00:54,347
degrees.

20
00:00:54,367 --> 00:00:54,918
That's all of it.

21
00:00:54,938 --> 00:00:56,346
Look those up when you need them.

22
00:00:56,366 --> 00:00:58,581
Everything else, you need to know cold.

23
00:00:58,641 --> 00:01:00,264
Part one, lines.

24
00:01:00,284 --> 00:01:03,371
Formula one is slope: y two minus y one,

25
00:01:03,391 --> 00:01:05,514
over x two minus x one.

26
00:01:05,534 --> 00:01:06,838
Rise over run.

27
00:01:06,858 --> 00:01:07,894
Example.

28
00:01:08,536 --> 00:01:11,409
A line passes through
the points negative two,

29
00:01:11,429 --> 00:01:14,231
seven, and four, negative five.

30
00:01:14,251 --> 00:01:16,358
What is the slope of the line?

31
00:01:16,383 --> 00:01:17,847
Pause and try it.

32
00:01:21,078 --> 00:01:23,665
The change in y is
negative five minus seven,

33
00:01:23,685 --> 00:01:25,043
or negative twelve.

34
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:28,165
The change in x is four
minus negative two,

35
00:01:28,185 --> 00:01:29,471
or six.

36
00:01:29,721 --> 00:01:32,487
Negative twelve over six is negative two.

37
00:01:32,507 --> 00:01:33,970
The answer is A.

38
00:01:34,012 --> 00:01:36,207
The traps are flipping
it to run over rise,

39
00:01:36,227 --> 00:01:38,262
and losing a negative sign.

40
00:01:38,369 --> 00:01:41,183
Subtract in the same
order on top and bottom.

41
00:01:41,203 --> 00:01:43,682
Formula two is three forms of a line.

42
00:01:43,702 --> 00:01:47,326
Slope-intercept: y equals m x plus b,

43
00:01:47,346 --> 00:01:50,468
where m is the slope and
b is the y intercept.

44
00:01:50,488 --> 00:01:55,183
Point-slope: y minus y one
equals m times x minus x one,

45
00:01:55,203 --> 00:01:57,632
for when you know a point and the slope.

46
00:01:57,699 --> 00:02:02,127
And standard form: A x plus B y equals C.

47
00:02:02,199 --> 00:02:05,072
Its slope is negative A over B.

48
00:02:05,092 --> 00:02:05,929
Example.

49
00:02:05,949 --> 00:02:10,072
A line has a slope of four and
passes through the point three,

50
00:02:10,092 --> 00:02:10,929
one.

51
00:02:10,949 --> 00:02:14,164
What is the y coordinate
of its y intercept?

52
00:02:14,195 --> 00:02:15,659
Pause and try it.

53
00:02:18,890 --> 00:02:19,942
Use point-slope.

54
00:02:19,962 --> 00:02:23,728
y minus one equals four
times x minus three.

55
00:02:23,748 --> 00:02:27,405
That's y minus one equals
four x minus twelve,

56
00:02:27,425 --> 00:02:30,390
so y equals four x minus eleven.

57
00:02:30,639 --> 00:02:32,934
The y intercept is negative eleven.

58
00:02:32,954 --> 00:02:34,077
Formula three.

59
00:02:34,097 --> 00:02:36,433
Parallel lines have equal slopes.

60
00:02:36,453 --> 00:02:39,684
Perpendicular lines have
negative reciprocal slopes:

61
00:02:39,704 --> 00:02:42,168
flip the fraction and change the sign.

62
00:02:42,219 --> 00:02:43,235
Example.

63
00:02:43,255 --> 00:02:48,362
Line p is defined by six x
minus two y equals seven.

64
00:02:48,469 --> 00:02:51,556
Line q is perpendicular to line p.

65
00:02:51,576 --> 00:02:53,719
What is the slope of line q?

66
00:02:53,761 --> 00:02:55,225
Pause and try it.

67
00:02:58,456 --> 00:03:03,293
Line p is in standard form, so
its slope is negative A over B:

68
00:03:03,313 --> 00:03:06,650
negative six over negative
two, which is three.

69
00:03:06,670 --> 00:03:09,920
Flip it and change the
sign: negative one third.

70
00:03:10,028 --> 00:03:11,705
The answer is B.

71
00:03:11,738 --> 00:03:13,504
Three is the parallel slope.

72
00:03:13,524 --> 00:03:17,952
Negative three and positive one
third each do only half the job.

73
00:03:17,972 --> 00:03:19,115
Formula four.

74
00:03:19,329 --> 00:03:22,579
Distance is the square
root of the change in x,

75
00:03:22,615 --> 00:03:25,059
squared, plus the change in y, squared.

76
00:03:25,079 --> 00:03:27,008
That's just the Pythagorean theorem.

77
00:03:27,043 --> 00:03:30,829
And the midpoint averages the
x values and the y values.

78
00:03:30,857 --> 00:03:31,857
Example.

79
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:35,837
Segment A B has endpoints
A at negative one,

80
00:03:35,857 --> 00:03:38,643
two, and B at five, ten.

81
00:03:38,822 --> 00:03:41,312
What is the length of segment A B?

82
00:03:41,332 --> 00:03:42,796
Pause and try it.

83
00:03:46,027 --> 00:03:47,400
The changes are six and eight.

84
00:03:47,420 --> 00:03:49,471
Six squared plus eight
squared is one hundred,

85
00:03:49,491 --> 00:03:51,650
and the square root of one hundred is ten.

86
00:03:51,670 --> 00:03:53,813
The midpoint is two, six.

87
00:03:53,884 --> 00:03:57,507
In Desmos, type distance, with
the two points in parentheses,

88
00:03:57,527 --> 00:03:58,777
and you get ten.

89
00:03:59,384 --> 00:04:01,294
Midpoint works the same way.

90
00:04:01,314 --> 00:04:03,242
Part two, quadratics.

91
00:04:03,813 --> 00:04:09,508
Formula five: for a x squared
plus b x plus c equals zero,

92
00:04:09,528 --> 00:04:15,758
x equals negative b, plus or minus the
square root of b squared minus four a c,

93
00:04:15,778 --> 00:04:17,371
all over two a.

94
00:04:17,391 --> 00:04:18,336
Example.

95
00:04:18,356 --> 00:04:23,407
Which of the following are the solutions
to two x squared minus four x minus

96
00:04:23,427 --> 00:04:24,926
three equals zero?

97
00:04:24,953 --> 00:04:26,417
Pause and try it.

98
00:04:29,648 --> 00:04:33,700
a is two, b is negative four,
and c is negative three.

99
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:36,164
Under the root: sixteen plus twenty-four,

100
00:04:36,184 --> 00:04:37,270
which is forty.

101
00:04:37,290 --> 00:04:40,592
So x equals four, plus
or minus root forty,

102
00:04:40,612 --> 00:04:41,641
over four.

103
00:04:41,661 --> 00:04:43,732
Root forty is two root ten.

104
00:04:43,767 --> 00:04:47,855
Divide every term by two:
two, plus or minus root ten,

105
00:04:47,875 --> 00:04:48,747
over two.

106
00:04:48,767 --> 00:04:50,268
The answer is C.

107
00:04:50,768 --> 00:04:55,411
D forgot to divide by two a, and A
used negative four for negative b.

108
00:04:55,446 --> 00:04:59,641
Formula six is the discriminant:
b squared minus four a c.

109
00:04:59,661 --> 00:05:01,676
Positive means two real solutions.

110
00:05:01,696 --> 00:05:03,498
Zero means exactly one.

111
00:05:03,518 --> 00:05:05,124
Negative means none.

112
00:05:05,144 --> 00:05:06,180
Example.

113
00:05:06,716 --> 00:05:10,910
In the equation x squared
plus ten x plus c equals zero,

114
00:05:10,930 --> 00:05:12,287
c is a constant.

115
00:05:12,786 --> 00:05:16,195
If the equation has
exactly one real solution,

116
00:05:16,215 --> 00:05:17,911
what is the value of c?

117
00:05:17,931 --> 00:05:19,395
Pause and try it.

118
00:05:22,626 --> 00:05:26,197
Exactly one solution means
the discriminant is zero.

119
00:05:26,376 --> 00:05:28,892
One hundred minus four c equals zero,

120
00:05:28,912 --> 00:05:30,769
so c is twenty-five.

121
00:05:30,843 --> 00:05:35,465
Desmos shortcut: graph y equals
x squared plus ten x plus c,

122
00:05:35,485 --> 00:05:37,430
and add a slider for c.

123
00:05:37,450 --> 00:05:40,823
The slider only runs from
negative ten to ten at first,

124
00:05:40,843 --> 00:05:42,965
so change its upper limit to fifty.

125
00:05:42,985 --> 00:05:46,180
Then drag until the parabola
just touches the x axis.

126
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:47,557
That's at twenty-five.

127
00:05:47,667 --> 00:05:49,647
Formula seven is the vertex.

128
00:05:49,667 --> 00:05:53,576
Its x coordinate is negative b over two a.

129
00:05:53,596 --> 00:05:55,112
Plug that in to get y.

130
00:05:55,132 --> 00:05:59,647
And in vertex form, y
equals a times x minus h,

131
00:05:59,667 --> 00:06:02,933
squared, plus k, the vertex is just h,

132
00:06:02,953 --> 00:06:03,573
k.

133
00:06:03,593 --> 00:06:04,573
Example.

134
00:06:04,593 --> 00:06:10,180
What is the vertex of the graph of y
equals two x squared plus twelve x plus

135
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:11,149
thirteen?

136
00:06:11,169 --> 00:06:12,633
Pause and try it.

137
00:06:15,865 --> 00:06:18,772
Negative twelve over
four is negative three.

138
00:06:18,792 --> 00:06:24,094
Plug it in: eighteen minus thirty-six
plus thirteen is negative five.

139
00:06:24,114 --> 00:06:27,166
The vertex is negative
three, negative five.

140
00:06:27,186 --> 00:06:28,793
The answer is D.

141
00:06:28,817 --> 00:06:32,475
Desmos check: graph it and
click the bottom of the curve.

142
00:06:32,495 --> 00:06:34,924
Desmos labels the vertex for you.

143
00:06:34,949 --> 00:06:40,072
Formula eight: for a x squared
plus b x plus c equals zero,

144
00:06:40,092 --> 00:06:42,679
the sum of the solutions
is negative b over a,

145
00:06:42,699 --> 00:06:45,664
and the product is c over a.

146
00:06:45,734 --> 00:06:47,056
No solving needed.

147
00:06:47,098 --> 00:06:48,098
Example.

148
00:06:48,455 --> 00:06:54,792
What is the product of the solutions
to two x squared plus nine x minus ten

149
00:06:54,812 --> 00:06:55,937
equals zero?

150
00:06:55,957 --> 00:06:57,421
Pause and try it.

151
00:07:00,652 --> 00:07:04,561
c over a is negative ten over
two, which is negative five.

152
00:07:04,581 --> 00:07:05,902
The answer is B.

153
00:07:05,974 --> 00:07:10,949
Negative nine halves is the sum, and
negative ten forgot to divide by a.

154
00:07:10,969 --> 00:07:13,576
Part three, circles and trig.

155
00:07:13,897 --> 00:07:18,342
Formula nine: x minus h,
squared, plus y minus k,

156
00:07:18,362 --> 00:07:20,699
squared, equals r squared.

157
00:07:20,719 --> 00:07:24,647
The center is h, k, and the radius is r.

158
00:07:24,755 --> 00:07:27,874
If the equation comes
expanded, complete the square.

159
00:07:27,894 --> 00:07:28,930
Example.

160
00:07:29,001 --> 00:07:33,874
The equation x squared plus y squared
plus eight x minus two y equals eight

161
00:07:33,894 --> 00:07:36,517
represents a circle in the x y plane.

162
00:07:36,537 --> 00:07:38,491
What is the radius of the circle?

163
00:07:38,511 --> 00:07:39,975
Pause and try it.

164
00:07:43,206 --> 00:07:47,242
Half of eight is four, and
four squared is sixteen.

165
00:07:47,313 --> 00:07:49,615
Half of negative two is negative one,

166
00:07:49,635 --> 00:07:51,528
and that squared is one.

167
00:07:51,598 --> 00:07:54,028
Add sixteen and one to both sides.

168
00:07:54,078 --> 00:07:57,557
Now it's x plus four,
squared, plus y minus one,

169
00:07:57,577 --> 00:07:59,201
squared, equals twenty-five.

170
00:07:59,221 --> 00:08:02,164
The radius is five, not twenty-five.

171
00:08:02,184 --> 00:08:05,701
The answer is C, and the
center is negative four,

172
00:08:05,721 --> 00:08:06,393
one.

173
00:08:06,413 --> 00:08:07,520
Formula ten.

174
00:08:08,377 --> 00:08:11,464
Arcs and sectors are
fractions of the circle.

175
00:08:11,484 --> 00:08:14,964
The fraction is the central
angle over three sixty.

176
00:08:14,984 --> 00:08:17,821
Multiply it by the
circumference for arc length,

177
00:08:17,841 --> 00:08:20,467
or by the area for sector area.

178
00:08:20,487 --> 00:08:21,558
Example.

179
00:08:21,665 --> 00:08:24,717
A circle has a radius of nine centimeters.

180
00:08:24,737 --> 00:08:27,788
What is the area, in square centimeters,

181
00:08:27,808 --> 00:08:31,165
of a sector with a central
angle of forty degrees?

182
00:08:31,234 --> 00:08:32,699
Pause and try it.

183
00:08:35,930 --> 00:08:37,874
Forty over three sixty is one ninth.

184
00:08:37,894 --> 00:08:41,624
The whole area is eighty-one
pi, so the sector is nine pi.

185
00:08:41,644 --> 00:08:43,087
The answer is B.

186
00:08:43,107 --> 00:08:46,500
Two pi is the arc length,
which is the common mix-up.

187
00:08:46,609 --> 00:08:49,922
If the angle is in radians,
compare it to two pi instead.

188
00:08:49,942 --> 00:08:51,371
Formula eleven.

189
00:08:51,941 --> 00:08:56,406
Soh-cah-toa: sine is
opposite over hypotenuse,

190
00:08:56,442 --> 00:09:02,065
cosine is adjacent over hypotenuse,
and tangent is opposite over adjacent.

191
00:09:02,085 --> 00:09:04,871
Always measured from the
angle the question names.

192
00:09:04,897 --> 00:09:05,897
Example.

193
00:09:05,968 --> 00:09:11,254
In right triangle X Y Z,
angle Z is the right angle.

194
00:09:11,397 --> 00:09:17,397
X Z is twenty-four, Y Z is
seven, and X Y is twenty-five.

195
00:09:17,539 --> 00:09:20,183
What is the value of cosine of X?

196
00:09:20,230 --> 00:09:21,694
Pause and try it.

197
00:09:24,925 --> 00:09:28,282
From angle X, the adjacent
side is twenty-four,

198
00:09:28,424 --> 00:09:30,782
and the hypotenuse is twenty-five.

199
00:09:30,818 --> 00:09:34,047
So cosine of X is
twenty-four over twenty-five.

200
00:09:34,067 --> 00:09:35,512
The answer is C.

201
00:09:35,532 --> 00:09:38,710
Seven over twenty-five is sine of X.

202
00:09:38,732 --> 00:09:43,784
Now notice: from angle Y, sine is
also twenty-four over twenty-five.

203
00:09:43,804 --> 00:09:44,927
That's the rule.

204
00:09:44,947 --> 00:09:49,497
Sine of x equals cosine
of ninety degrees minus x,

205
00:09:49,517 --> 00:09:52,445
because the two acute
angles add up to ninety.

206
00:09:52,465 --> 00:09:53,481
Example.

207
00:09:53,501 --> 00:09:58,266
If sine of x degrees equals
cosine of thirty-two degrees,

208
00:09:58,286 --> 00:10:03,179
and x is between zero and
ninety, what is the value of x?

209
00:10:03,226 --> 00:10:04,690
Pause and try it.

210
00:10:07,921 --> 00:10:10,187
Ninety minus thirty-two is fifty-eight.

211
00:10:10,207 --> 00:10:14,401
To check in Desmos, switch
to degrees in graph settings,

212
00:10:14,421 --> 00:10:18,884
then type sine of fifty-eight
and cosine of thirty-two.

213
00:10:18,992 --> 00:10:20,089
Same decimal.

214
00:10:20,109 --> 00:10:22,053
Part four, exponents.

215
00:10:22,073 --> 00:10:24,268
Formula twelve is a set of rules.

216
00:10:24,288 --> 00:10:26,232
Multiplying, add the exponents.

217
00:10:26,252 --> 00:10:27,802
Dividing, subtract them.

218
00:10:27,822 --> 00:10:29,803
Power of a power, multiply them.

219
00:10:29,823 --> 00:10:32,108
A negative exponent means one over.

220
00:10:32,215 --> 00:10:36,502
And in a fraction exponent, the top is
the power and the bottom is the root.

221
00:10:36,548 --> 00:10:37,548
Example.

222
00:10:37,655 --> 00:10:43,099
Which expression is equivalent to
the quantity three x to the fourth,

223
00:10:43,119 --> 00:10:46,063
squared, times x to the negative five,

224
00:10:46,083 --> 00:10:47,860
where x is not zero?

225
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:49,344
Pause and try it.

226
00:10:52,575 --> 00:10:55,054
Squaring gives nine x to the eighth.

227
00:10:55,074 --> 00:10:57,519
Then multiply by x to the negative five,

228
00:10:57,539 --> 00:11:01,341
so add the exponents:
eight minus five is three.

229
00:11:01,361 --> 00:11:03,003
That's nine x cubed.

230
00:11:03,182 --> 00:11:04,825
The answer is A.

231
00:11:05,074 --> 00:11:08,075
C doubled the three
instead of squaring it.

232
00:11:08,096 --> 00:11:09,418
Formula thirteen.

233
00:11:09,560 --> 00:11:14,648
Growth: y equals a times
the quantity one plus r,

234
00:11:14,668 --> 00:11:15,668
to the t.

235
00:11:15,738 --> 00:11:17,968
For decay, it's one minus r.

236
00:11:17,988 --> 00:11:21,872
a is the starting amount, and
r is the percent as a decimal.

237
00:11:21,892 --> 00:11:22,943
Example.

238
00:11:22,963 --> 00:11:25,872
A machine was worth five thousand
dollars when it was bought,

239
00:11:25,892 --> 00:11:29,336
and its value decreases
by ten percent each year.

240
00:11:29,356 --> 00:11:32,479
Which function gives
its value V, in dollars,

241
00:11:32,499 --> 00:11:34,356
t years after it was bought?

242
00:11:34,426 --> 00:11:35,891
Pause and try it.

243
00:11:39,122 --> 00:11:41,816
Losing ten percent means
keeping ninety percent,

244
00:11:41,836 --> 00:11:43,888
so the multiplier is point nine.

245
00:11:43,908 --> 00:11:45,979
The answer is D.

246
00:11:46,193 --> 00:11:49,208
B keeps only ten percent, C is growth,

247
00:11:49,228 --> 00:11:50,841
and A is linear.

248
00:11:50,861 --> 00:11:55,448
After two years, the machine is
worth four thousand fifty dollars,

249
00:11:55,468 --> 00:11:56,770
not four thousand.

250
00:11:56,790 --> 00:11:59,912
Each year takes ten percent
of a smaller amount.

251
00:11:59,932 --> 00:12:03,697
In Desmos, use x for t, define f of x,

252
00:12:03,717 --> 00:12:06,037
and type f of two to check.

253
00:12:06,057 --> 00:12:08,914
Part five, percents and stats.

254
00:12:09,021 --> 00:12:13,073
Formula fourteen: percent
change is new minus old,

255
00:12:13,093 --> 00:12:15,394
over old, times one hundred.

256
00:12:15,414 --> 00:12:18,930
From forty dollars to
thirty-four is a six-dollar drop,

257
00:12:18,950 --> 00:12:22,700
and six over forty is a
fifteen percent decrease.

258
00:12:22,791 --> 00:12:25,056
The SAT also runs it backward.

259
00:12:25,076 --> 00:12:26,163
Example.

260
00:12:26,183 --> 00:12:30,699
After a twenty percent discount, a
jacket costs forty-eight dollars.

261
00:12:30,719 --> 00:12:33,112
What was the original price of the jacket?

262
00:12:33,177 --> 00:12:34,641
Pause and try it.

263
00:12:37,872 --> 00:12:40,372
Twenty percent off means
you pay eighty percent.

264
00:12:40,479 --> 00:12:42,602
Point eight times the
price is forty-eight,

265
00:12:42,622 --> 00:12:44,281
so the price is sixty dollars.

266
00:12:44,301 --> 00:12:45,575
The answer is C.

267
00:12:45,595 --> 00:12:48,289
The trap is B, adding twenty
percent of forty-eight.

268
00:12:48,309 --> 00:12:52,003
But the discount came
off the original price,

269
00:12:52,023 --> 00:12:53,558
not the sale price.

270
00:12:53,626 --> 00:12:57,841
Formula fifteen: the mean is
the sum divided by the count.

271
00:12:58,198 --> 00:13:03,580
The version the SAT really wants
is total equals mean times count.

272
00:13:03,600 --> 00:13:04,473
Example.

273
00:13:04,493 --> 00:13:07,402
The mean of a student's five
test scores is eighty-two.

274
00:13:07,422 --> 00:13:12,508
What score on a sixth test would make
the mean of all six scores equal to

275
00:13:12,528 --> 00:13:13,488
eighty-four?

276
00:13:13,508 --> 00:13:14,972
Pause and try it.

277
00:13:18,203 --> 00:13:22,326
Five scores averaging eighty-two
total four hundred ten.

278
00:13:22,346 --> 00:13:26,560
Six scores averaging eighty-four
total five hundred four.

279
00:13:26,775 --> 00:13:28,702
The difference is ninety-four.

280
00:13:28,882 --> 00:13:31,182
Whenever values are added or removed,

281
00:13:31,202 --> 00:13:32,525
switch to totals.

282
00:13:32,545 --> 00:13:35,882
On test day, trigger words
tell you which formula to use.

283
00:13:35,902 --> 00:13:38,204
Perpendicular: negative reciprocal.

284
00:13:38,224 --> 00:13:40,973
Exactly one solution: discriminant.

285
00:13:41,080 --> 00:13:44,847
Sum or product of the
solutions: negative b over a,

286
00:13:44,867 --> 00:13:46,203
or c over a.

287
00:13:46,223 --> 00:13:48,617
Maximum or minimum: vertex.

288
00:13:48,649 --> 00:13:51,272
Center or radius: complete the square.

289
00:13:51,292 --> 00:13:54,272
Percent per year: one plus or minus r,

290
00:13:54,292 --> 00:13:55,292
to the t.

291
00:13:55,434 --> 00:13:58,022
A mean with a value added or removed:

292
00:13:58,042 --> 00:13:58,772
totals.

293
00:13:58,792 --> 00:14:01,531
And if it's on the reference
sheet, just open the sheet.

294
00:14:01,551 --> 00:14:03,031
That's all fifteen on one screen.

295
00:14:03,051 --> 00:14:04,822
Pause here if you want a screenshot.

296
00:14:04,842 --> 00:14:08,036
Every example here was
written for this video,

297
00:14:08,056 --> 00:14:10,465
in the style of the real test.

298
